# Laravel + React Consistency

## Backend

- Prefer constructor DI; never `app(Service::class)` inside methods unless resolving strategy/factories.
- Authorize with `$this->authorize(...)` or Request `authorize()` before service calls.
- Domain exceptions in `app/Modules/...` or `app/Shared/Exceptions`; map in the exception handler by `$request->wantsJson()`.
- Feature tests cover cross-user isolation on both web and api routes.
- Do not put module code in legacy `app/Http/Controllers` — use `app/Modules/{Module}/Controllers`.
- Migrations are the schema source of truth; no ad-hoc SQL for app features.

## Frontend

- Colocate feature UI under `Components/{module}/` mirroring backend modules (`brand`, `assets`, `folders`).
- Shared helpers in `lib/`; do not duplicate Axios/CSRF setup.
- Show Laravel/Inertia `errors` field messages next to inputs; do not invent parallel client-only error models for server rules.
- Avoid prop drilling beyond one level — use page props or small context only when needed.
- No `any` in new TypeScript; prefer `unknown` + narrowing if needed.

## Security

- Never expose AI API keys or secrets to the React bundle.
- Treat all client payloads as untrusted; re-validate AI suggestion shape on save server-side.
